00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.590
From the transfer perspective,
what that means is

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.380
we want to make sure that
your data is delivered

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.660
where and when you
need it so that you

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.670
can make it useful
for your workloads

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.800
and for your business.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.460
Now, there are a lot of
different applications

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.050
