00:02:00.408 --> 00:02:02.200
And then maybe let's
say you've figured out

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.825
what data you want to move, but
you don't have enough bandwidth

00:02:04.825 --> 00:02:06.560
to move it.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.639
Or maybe you've done
both of these things,

00:02:08.639 --> 00:02:11.370
but now getting access
to data is the problem.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.560
It's behind a firewall.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.365
You need to get
internal approvals.

00:02:14.365 --> 00:02:15.740
These are all
challenges that you

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:18.110
have to face when
you're moving your data.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:19.760
And then finally,
sometimes you just

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.110
may not have the org resources.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.510
There's nobody available
to actually say, move

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.530
the data now.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:28.460
What we aim to do with
our transfer product suite

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.590
is to provide you
a set of solutions

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:33.680
that are simple,
reliable, and secure,

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.110
and hopefully,
remove or at least

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:40.880
